{{Han simp|僞|f=爲|t=為}}. {{Han compound|人|alt1=亻|為|t1=man|t2=to make|ls=psc|c1=s|c2=p}}, originally “artificial”.

===Etymology===
Often thought to be derived from {{och-l|為|id=1|to act as}} ({{zh-ref|Karlgren, 1956}}; {{zh-ref|Wang, 1982}}; {{zh-ref|Baxter and Sagart, 2014}}).

Alternatively, it may be cognate to {{och-l|訛|erroneous}} ({{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}); this may be compared to {{cog|bo|རྔོད||to deceive}}, though the ''-d'' in Tibetan is unexplained ({{zh-ref|Gong, 1995}}; {{zh-ref|Schuessler, 2007}}; {{zh-ref|Hill, 2014}}).

{{zh-ref|Jacques (2022, 2023)}} seems to attempt to unify the two etymologies above. He argues the {{cog|ltc|-}} initial ''ng-'' in both {{ltc-l|偽}} and {{ltc-l|訛}} come from a middle voice/intransitivizing prefix {{m|und|*ŋ-}}. {{lang|zh|偽}}, reconstructed as {{m|und|*ŋ-waj-s}}, would be derived from {{och-l|為|tr=waj}} as the root.

